worked out, as Peaty won gold in a stunning world record 57.13, winning by more than 1½ seconds over van der Bergh, with Miller winning a slightly surprising bronze, as he had not been heard from much before 2016. Peaty had actually broken his world record of 57.92 in the sixth heat, finishing in 57.55, then shattering that in the final. In all, he lowered the pre-Rio world mark by 0.79 seconds, a huge margin at this distance, and his record was 1.33 seconds ahead of the second fastest performer of all-time, van der Bergh."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/134063"} "Adam Peaty"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "57.55 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "57.62 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "57.13 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/112223"} "Cameron van der Burgh"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RSA.png"}] "RSA"]] [:td {} "59.35 (2 h5)"] [:td {} "59.21 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "58.69 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136357"} "Cody Miller"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "59.17 (3 h4)"] [:td {} "59.05 (2 h2)"] [:td {} "58.87 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Br